Article 11: A commissioning document for expert evaluation shall contain clear evaluation matters and evaluation requirements. The expert shall conduct the evaluation in accordance with the commissioned evaluation matters and requirements.
The following specialized issues may serve as matters for applying for medical damage expert evaluation:
(1) Whether there is fault in the performance of diagnosis and treatment;
(2) Whether there is a causal relationship between the diagnosis and treatment behavior and the damage consequence, and the degree of causative potency;
(3) Whether the medical institution fulfilled its obligation of explanation and the obligation to obtain explicit consent from the patient or the patient's close relatives;
(4) Whether a medical product has defects, whether there is a causal relationship between the defects and the damage consequence, and the degree of causative potency;
(5) The degree of the patient's injury and disability;
(6) The patient's nursing period, rest period, and nutritional period;
(7) Other specialized issues.
Evaluation requirements include the qualifications of the expert, the composition of the expert panel, the evaluation procedure, the evaluation opinion, and the evaluation time limit.

Article 18: Where, due to an emergency such as rescuing a patient whose life is in critical danger and the patient's opinion cannot be obtained, the following circumstances may be determined as the inability to obtain the opinions of the patient's close relatives as provided in Article 1220 of the Civil Code:
(1) The close relatives are unknown;
(2) The close relatives cannot be contacted in a timely manner;
(3) The close relatives refuse to give opinions;
(4) The close relatives cannot reach a unanimous opinion;
(5) Other circumstances provided by laws and regulations.
In the circumstances of the preceding paragraph, where medical personnel, with the approval of the person in charge of the medical institution or an authorized person in charge, immediately implement the corresponding medical measures, and the patient thereby requests the medical institution to bear compensation liability, such request shall not be supported; where the medical institution and its medical personnel negligently fail to implement the corresponding medical measures, causing damage, and the patient requests the medical institution to bear compensation liability, such request shall be supported.

Article 24: Where an infringed party simultaneously prosecutes two or more medical institutions to bear compensation liability, and the People's Court finds after trial that the medical institution located at the place of the court accepting the case does not bear compensation liability according to law, while other medical institutions bear compensation liability, the calculation of disability compensation and death compensation shall be handled separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) If one medical institution bears liability, the compensation standard of the place where that medical institution is located shall apply;
(2) If two or more medical institutions all bear liability, the standard of the place where the medical institution with the higher compensation standard is located may be applied.
